description:
FILED s543l (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the reviewing session's L3 (review of s543l, probes-1127/rl2/p/z-05.pl); base = tree.  No task owned it (searched: #1029 #1873 #2108 #2374 #5333 #5380 -- the __DIE__ / signal neighbourhood).

A `die` raised inside a signal handler calls `$SIG{__DIE__}` TWICE in perl -- once at the die inside the handler, once more when perl re-raises it out of the signal dispatch (Perl_sighandler's die_sv of ERRSV) -- and ONCE under PCL.  The $@ the eval sees is the same ("h").

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl):
    $| = 1; $SIG{USR1} = sub { die "h\n" };
    { local $SIG{__DIE__} = sub { print "DIEHOOK $_[0]" }; eval { kill USR1 => $$; sleep 1 }; print "[", $@ =~ s/\n//r, "]\n"; }
    $SIG{ALRM} = sub { die "al\n" };
    { local $SIG{__DIE__} = sub { print "DH3 $_[0]" }; eval { alarm 1; sleep 3 }; print "[", $@ =~ s/\n//r, "]\n"; }
  perl: DIEHOOK h / DIEHOOK h / [h] / DH3 al / DH3 al / [al]
  PCL:  DIEHOOK h / [h] / DH3 al / [al]
  A plain `die` in an eval: one call in both (right).

DIRECTION (not built): the delivery (%p-sig-deliver's :handler arm) re-raises a Perl die that leaves the handler through the die hook once more (perl's second call), with *p-in-die-handler* as perl's PL_diehook guard.  Measure first whether the second call sees the same message object.

FREQUENCY: rare -- a __DIE__ hook that prints or counts while a signal handler dies (a logging hook under an alarm timeout would print the line twice in perl); known from the review probe only.
